# Copy to .leakterms.local (gitignored) and list anything that must never be
# published. One term per line, case-insensitive, matched on word boundaries.
#
# Be exhaustive and err toward over-listing. The built-in patterns catch
# structural leaks (paths, tokens, register citations); this list is the only
# thing that catches named ones, and the terms people forget are the ones they
# do not think of as sensitive.
#
# Work through these categories rather than listing from memory:
#   your name, and every other real person you write about
#   your vault's own folder name
#   project, venture, employer and client names
#   private life-domain folders — health, family, spiritual practice, journals,
#     identity work, finance, sport, anything you would not show a stranger
#   any `type:` value naming a private practice
#   product or accelerator names used as examples
#
# Your-Name
# Your-Vault
# ProjectCodename
#
# Path exemptions: a line starting with ! is a glob of files to skip.
# Use sparingly — each one is a file nobody is checking any more.
# The canonical case is a copyright line, which must name a real person.
#
# !LICENSE
